    "class": "gps-598687487451202103 gps gpsil",
    "settings": [{"type":"paragraph","content":"Section design by GemPages. [Click here to start design](https://admin.shopify.com/store/e49d78-3/apps/gempages-cro/app/shopify/edit?pageType=GP_PRE_SALE_PAGE&editorId=598687178498769463&sectionId=598687487451202103)"},{"type":"select","label":"Section Preload","id":"section_preload","options":[{"label":"On","value":"true"},{"label":"Off","value":"false"},{"label":"Off Lazy Script","value":"off_lazy_script"}],"default":"false"},{"type":"text","label":"Checksum","id":"checksum"},{"type":"html","id":"gg8Jxmf75Nm_text","label":"gg8Jxmf75Nm_text","default":"<p>#1 TRENDING IN MEN'S VITALITY</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggcyHitKNBs_text","label":"ggcyHitKNBs_text","default":"THE \"GHOST\" IN THE KITCHEN: Why Successful Men Are Hiding From Their Own Lives (And Why It’s Not Depression—It’s Starvation)"},{"type":"html","id":"gg4jf8-ZVaS_srcSet_desktop_src","label":"gg4jf8-ZVaS_srcSet_desktop_src","default":"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0810/1563/6283/files/ChatGPT_Image_Aug_19_2025_05_02_49_PM_100x100_69d0e32d-b9c2-4bd1-acee-b546bcd87f2b.webp"},{"type":"html","id":"ggR5ZrS9Slv_text","label":"ggR5ZrS9Slv_text","default":"<p>By <strong>Daniel Reyes</strong> | July 17, 2025 | Health &amp; Performance</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggva3IY3K7F_text","label":"ggva3IY3K7F_text","default":"<p>Estimated 8-10 Minutes Read</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gggZhIRteg__srcSet_desktop_src","label":"gggZhIRteg__srcSet_desktop_src","default":"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0810/1563/6283/files/1765348719-Marcus_4.webp"},{"type":"html","id":"ggAEzqmPX_8_text","label":"ggAEzqmPX_8_text","default":"<p>Monday, 6:40 AM.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Marcus stared at the half-empty tub of pre-workout on his kitchen counter — the same one he bought two months ago and still hadn't finished. He used to feel something when he took it. A spark. A push. Now it was just... noise. A brief buzz, then nothing. By noon, the crash would hit. By 3 PM, he'd be running on fumes and willpower.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>It wasn't supposed to be like this.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>At 38, Marcus wasn't old. He'd been a regional sales director in Charlotte for six years — the kind of guy who used to arrive early and leave late because he wanted to, not because he had to. He ate reasonably well. He still made it to the gym—when he could drag himself there. He slept... enough. On paper, everything looked fine.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>But something had shifted. Something he couldn't name.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>It wasn't pain. It wasn't illness. It was quieter than that—a slow dimming he only noticed when he tried to remember what \"normal\" used to feel like.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The drive wasn't there. The edge. That feeling of waking up ready to attack the day. He'd look in the mirror and see someone he didn't quite recognize—softer, slower, duller than the man he used to be.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>His wife noticed. She didn't say anything, but he could tell. The way she looked at him.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The weekends they used to fill with plans that now just... passed.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>He wasn't chasing miracles. He just wanted to feel like himself again.</p><p>If this sounds familiar, you're not alone.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Millions of men hit their mid-30s and start asking the same question Marcus did: \"Why do I feel so drained? Why doesn't anything work anymore?\"</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The answer isn't what you think.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>There's a version of yourself you remember.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The one who woke up ready. Who walked into rooms and felt like he belonged there.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Who didn't have to talk himself into getting through the afternoon.</p><p>You're not asking for superpowers. You just want that version back.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Here's the truth most men never hear:</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggz7Sy5oOsK_srcSet_desktop_src","label":"ggz7Sy5oOsK_srcSet_desktop_src","default":"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0810/1563/6283/files/1765348893-Marcus_8.webp"},{"type":"html","id":"ggC1k35N-C__text","label":"ggC1k35N-C__text","default":"It's Not Age. It's Depletion"},{"type":"html","id":"ggfEJ_jXaj-_text","label":"ggfEJ_jXaj-_text","default":"<p>After 35, something shifts in your body. Not dramatically—not all at once—but quietly. Steadily. Like a slow leak you don't notice until the tank is nearly empty.</p><p>Your energy slips. Not \"normal tired\"—rest doesn't refill the tank anymore.</p><p>Your drive fades. Even after a full night's sleep, mornings feel flat. Workouts stall. That fire you used to have? Gone.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Your focus wavers. Fog creeps in. Patience shortens. Evenings feel wasted.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>But here's what most men—and most doctors—don't realize:</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The problem isn't your testosterone levels. It's what your body needs to PRODUCE testosterone in the first place.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Not protein. Not carbs. Not another supplement with 47 ingredients you can't pronounce.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>It's trace minerals. The raw materials your body has been starved of since the soil your food grows in was stripped bare by industrial farming.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>And once you understand this, everything changes.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggGOOvr6Mh__srcSet_desktop_src","label":"ggGOOvr6Mh__srcSet_desktop_src","default":"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0810/1563/6283/files/1765350023-332944b6-9d12-42dd-bfdb-c10f11177071.webp"},{"type":"html","id":"ggm1ZWvaN-2_text","label":"ggm1ZWvaN-2_text","default":"Why Everything You've Tried Has Failed"},{"type":"html","id":"ggFKs8CpF5j_text","label":"ggFKs8CpF5j_text","default":"<p>You've probably cycled through the usual suspects:</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggCZH_SXl57_text","label":"ggCZH_SXl57_text","default":"<p>☕ <strong>Coffee and caffeine</strong> — a spike, then a crash, then dependency</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>💊 <strong>Generic multivitamins</strong> — broad claims, weak effects, zero change</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>🧪 <strong>Pre-workouts and energy drinks</strong> — jitters, heart racing, still exhausted by noon</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>💉 <strong>Maybe you've even considered TRT</strong> — but the idea of needles, doctor visits, and lifelong dependency stopped you</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggtCCaaeyN4_text","label":"ggtCCaaeyN4_text","default":"<p>Here's the hard truth: <strong>None of these address the root cause.</strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>They're all chasing symptoms. Patching holes. Masking the problem while it gets worse.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The supplement industry doesn't want to fix you. They want to keep you buying.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>That's why most \"testosterone boosters\" are stuffed with underdosed herbs that look good on a label but do nothing in your body.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>That's why energy drinks give you a two-hour window of fake productivity followed by a crash that makes you worse than before.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>That's why you've spent hundreds—maybe thousands—of dollars and still feel exactly the same.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>There is another way.</strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>What Marcus didn't know was that the answer wasn't in his supplement cabinet. It was 7,000 miles away — in a mountain range older than human civilization.</p>"}],
    "blocks": [{"type": "@app"}],
    "locales": {}
